      "title": "Adjunct Position, Department of Economics and Business Management, Agnes Scott College",
      "description": "Adjunct Position, Department of Economics and Business Management, Agnes Scott College | Agnes Scott College Cookie Notice This website uses cookies.  Find out more in our Privacy Policy . Got It! Close Agnes Scott College Search Agnes Scott Stories Events News Request Info Visit Apply Give Undergraduate Graduate & Post-Baccalaureate Physician Assistant Studies Undergraduate Graduate & Post-Baccalaureate Undergraduate Agnes Accelerated 4+1 Post-Baccalaureate Graduate Menu Search agnesscott.edu Submit Top searches Majors & Minors Graduate Programs Tuition Scholarships SUMMIT Faculty Directory Alumnae About SUMMIT Academics Admission & Aid Campus Life Athletics Graduate & Post-Bacc Studies Info for Current Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Donors Partners Parents & Families Agnes Scott College > Careers at Agnes Scott > Faculty Openings > Adjunct Position, Department of Economics and Business Management, Agnes Scott College Adjunct Position, Department of Economics and Business Management, Agnes Scott College Position: Adjunct Position, Department of Economics and Business Management Type: Non-tenure-track Faculty Department/Program: Department of Economics and Business Management The Department of Economics and Business Management at Agnes Scott College invites applications for an adjunct faculty position in spring semester 2027. The adjunct faculty member will be responsible for teaching one section of ECO206: Intermediate Microeconomics. This course typically enrolls 10-15 students. A Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree is required for the position; however, MA, MS, and ABD candidates will also be considered for appointment at the adjunct instructor level. Candidates must demonstrate evidence of excellence or the promise of excellence in teaching at the college level. Applicants should submit a letter of interest and a curriculum vitae to Tom Will (Department Chair) at twill@agnesscott.edu. Official graduate transcripts will be required prior to hiring. Please note that, in accordance with college policy, candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. About Agnes Scott College: Agnes Scott College is a highly selective, independent national liberal arts college for women, located in metropolitan Atlanta. As an equal opportunity employer, Agnes Scott College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, gender identity, gender expression, or any other characteristic protected by law in its employment practices. Back to top Agnes Scott College 141 E. College Ave. Decatur, Georgia 30030 Maps & Directions Contact us Site Index Directory Careers at Agnes Scott Event Rentals Consumer Information News Bradley Observatory Bookstores The Dalton Gallery McCain Library Support Agnes Scott Your support of the college is more valuable than ever as we address the known needs of today and anticipate what may come tomorrow. Make a Gift Partner with Us Agnes Scott College instagram Agnes Scott College TikTok Agnes Scott College facebook Agnes Scott College youtube Agnes Scott College linkedin © 2026 Agnes Scott College. All rights reserved. Privacy Title IX Accreditation Nondiscrimination Statement"
